mapping "V3293.1" source="V3293" target="274913009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V3293 is a Swedish ICD-10-SE 5th-character extension of parent ICD-10 V32.9 (V32.9 =
        unspecified occupant of three-wheeled motor vehicle injured in traffic collision with
        two-/three-wheeled motor vehicle); the 5th digit adds a Swedish SNOMED CT 274913009 36198007 axis
        (sport/work/leisure/vital activity) absent from the standard V-code and with no separate SNOMED CT
        representation. Parent V32.9 has an Athena crosswalk to SNOMED CT 433930 (Motor vehicle on road in
        collision with another motor vehicle); 444074 (Victim of vehicular AND/OR traffic accident). The
        parent's SNOMED CT target fully subsumes the clinical meaning (vehicle-occupant injury in a
        collision of this type); the activity axis is administrative context, not a clinical
        distinction, so target is broader. moderate: Athena crosswalk inherited from the parent,
        source-extension specificity (activity context) not independently re-verified in SNOMED CT.
        """
}
mapping "V3293.2" source="V3293" target="36198007" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
}
